# Git push — reactwoo-api-manager

Remotes:

| Remote | URL | Purpose |
|--------|-----|---------|
| `origin` | `ssh://reactwoo@reactwoo.com/home/reactwoo/public_html/wp-content/plugins/reactwoo-api-manager` | **Production deploy** |
| `github` | `https://github.com/reactwoo/reactwoo-api-manager.git` | Source control / backup |

## Agents

- **Commit** workspace/plugin changes when the user asks.
- **Do not** `git push origin` unless the user explicitly requests a **production deploy**.
- Pushing `origin` opens **SSH to reactwoo.com** and may prompt for a key/passphrase.
- When the user asks to push to GitHub, use `git push github main` (or the requested branch). Do not replace `origin` with GitHub.

## Packaging

- Local zip: `npm run package:zip` → `scripts/package_zip.py` (version-suffixed locally).
- Do not commit generated `*.zip` files.

## Product releases (Geo suite, Flow, LinkedIn, etc.)

Those repos use tagged GitHub R2 publishes. This plugin is storefront infrastructure — not an R2 customer plugin update.